3-OU5HX2XE.svg?dpl=3Ddpl_CEjisbLnWxFQGUTRjiHGoKY1oV5c"></div></figure>
<p>We=E2=80=99re still left with some questions. In particular, how can we =
tell if a square is being attacked, and how exactly do we =E2=80=9Cplace=E2=
=80=9D or =E2=80=9Cremove=E2=80=9D a queen?</p>
<p><strong>Detecting opposing queens</strong><br>
<!-- -->One challenge in this problem is determining if a square is attacke=
d by another queen. We could do a linear search across the row, column, and=
